# ChroniQ Backend Architecture & Design Decisions

This document records the architectural and data model decisions made to address all open questions, frontend integrations, and known gaps between `ChroniQ.md` (Specification) and the React frontend implementations (`frontend/src/services/*.ts`, `frontend/src/types/index.ts`).

---

## 1. Consultation Notes & Prescriptions
- **Decision**: Implemented as a dedicated Beanie Document model `ConsultationNote` in collection `consultation_notes`.
- **Fields**:
  - `appointment_id` (`PydanticObjectId`, indexed, unique per consultation)
  - `doctor_id` (`PydanticObjectId`)
  - `patient_id` (`PydanticObjectId`)
  - `text` (`str`)
  - `follow_up` (`str`: `none` | `1_week` | `2_weeks` | `1_month` | `custom`)
  - `follow_up_date` (`Optional[datetime]`)
  - `finalized` (`bool`: set to `True` upon consultation completion, locking edits)
  - `updated_at` (`datetime`)
- **API Endpoint**: `POST /consultations/draft` updates or creates an in-progress consultation note while the doctor conducts the consultation.

---

## 2. Doctor Availability State & Logs
- **Decision**: Implemented in collection `doctor_availability` and `availability_logs`.
- **State Fields**:
  - `doctor_id` (`PydanticObjectId`, unique)
  - `status` (`available` | `on_break` | `late` | `on_leave`)
  - `until` (`Optional[str]` - time or ISO string)
  - `delay_minutes` (`int`: default 0)
  - `reason` (`Optional[str]`)
  - `changed_at` (`datetime`)
- **Behavior**:
  - When status changes to `on_break` or `late`, downstream queue ETAs for waiting patients of that doctor automatically shift by `delay_minutes` (or duration of the break).
  - An event is emitted via SSE (`doctor_availability_changed`) so live patient queues and admin dashboards update instantly.
  - An entry is appended to `availability_logs`.

